    <bpmn:process id="W_W1735" name="W1735. Data Privacy Governance &amp; NPC Compliance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Data Privacy Act (RA 10173) compliance requirement; new data processing activity; NPC audit; data breach
Frequency: Continuous governance; annual review; event-driven for breaches
Volume: Ongoing compliance for 600,000 customer records + 6,925 employee records + vendor data
Owner: Data Protection Officer (DPO)
Participants: DPO, CIO, Legal Counsel, Corporate Secretary, all department heads
Source: workflow W1735 — Data Privacy Governance &amp; NPC Compliance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1735_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1735_Lane1" name="DPO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1735_End9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1735_Start3" name="Data Privacy Act (RA 10173) compliance requirement; new data processing activity; NPC…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1735_Task4" name="DPO maintains data privacy governance framework: (a) privacy policy (external —…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: DPO maintains data privacy governance framework: (a) privacy policy (external — for customers), (b) data protection policy (internal — for employees), (c) data processing agreements with all third-party service providers, (d) privacy impact assessments for new systems/processes, (e) data retention and disposal schedule, (f) breach notification procedure, (g) consent management for customer data collection
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1735_Task5" name="NPC registration: (a) DPO registered with National Privacy Commission…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: NPC registration: (a) DPO registered with National Privacy Commission (mandatory per RA 10173), (b) data processing systems registered with NPC, (c) annual renewal of registration
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): Corporate Secretary
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1735_Task6" name="Consent management: (a) loyalty program members: consent for data collection…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Consent management: (a) loyalty program members: consent for data collection, marketing communications, profiling, (b) ecommerce customers: privacy notice at checkout, cookie consent, data sharing consent, (c) employees: consent for processing SSS/PhilHealth/Pag-IBIG data, CCTV monitoring, biometric data, (d) vendors: consent for financial data processing
Responsible (R): DPO / Marketing / HR / Procurement
Accountable (A): DPO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1735_Task7" name="Data breach response (if triggered): (a) within 72 hours: initial assessment…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Data breach response (if triggered): (a) within 72 hours: initial assessment, containment, NPC notification (if involving sensitive personal information affecting 100+ data subjects), (b) within 5 days: full breach report to NPC, (c) affected data subjects notified, (d) remedial measures implemented, (e) post-incident review
Responsible (R): DPO / IT / Legal Counsel
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Event-driven</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1735_Task8" name="Annual privacy audit: DPO conducts internal review of data processing…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Annual privacy audit: DPO conducts internal review of data processing practices; findings reported to Audit Committee; corrective actions tracked
Responsible (R): DPO
Accountable (A): Audit Committee
Duration: 1–2 weeks/year</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1735_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1735_End9" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1735_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1735_Annotation10">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-351 (ensure controlled execution — Corporate Policy &amp; Entity Governance (PA-36.3).) | - operational: Data Protection Officer (DPO) review and approval gate
Owner: Data Protection Officer (DPO)</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
